    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Dingo',
            subtitle: 'Cleveland Hunt Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Dingo is a strategic card game for four players from Cleveland, Ohio. The game features a unique 'hunt' mechanic where diamonds (rabbits) are hunted in ascending order, with hearts (dingoes) and black cards (wolves) playing special roles. Players score points based on card values and hunt outcomes.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Country/Region of Origin: Cleveland, Ohio, USA\nTime Period: Several years prior to 2017 documentation\nHistorical Development: Played in card game circles in Cleveland\nCultural Significance: Part of Cleveland's unique card game culture along with Democracy and Ribs",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 4\nMaximum Players: 4\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: None - individual play',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Type: Standard 52-card deck with special classifications\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included\nSpecial classifications:\n- Diamonds = 'rabbits' (Ace of diamonds = 'Ace rabbit')\n- Hearts = 'dingoes'\n- Spades and Clubs = 'wolves'",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck\nTable space for rabbit pile and discards\nScore sheet',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'First dealer chosen randomly, passes left after each game\nDealer separates diamonds from deck (except Ace of diamonds stays in main pack)\nDiamonds 2-K ordered low to high, placed face up in center (2 on top)\nMain pack: 40 cards (13 hearts, 13 spades, 13 clubs, 1 Ace of diamonds)\nShuffle and deal 10 cards to each player',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'First to Five Games: Play a match where first player to win five games wins the match.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Running Total 100: Keep cumulative points across games; first to 100 points wins.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Conservative Ace Hunt: Table-specific ace-hunt play order and wolf timing conventions by prior agreement.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
